From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alpha-build <alpha-build@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:11:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Snap: do not hide the camera icon based on a boot-time
 Camera1 check

The DisableCameraReceiver ran on BOOT_COMPLETED, called the Camera 1
getNumberOfCameras(), saw 0 on this device and disabled
com.android.camera.CameraLauncher permanently - so after a fresh flash the
Camera app had no launcher entry even though both cameras work (Gallery
reached it through IMAGE_CAPTURE, a different component). The receiver also
set the camera2 mode, but CameraActivity does exactly the same at every
start, so dropping the boot trigger changes nothing else.

Change-Id: I4d04aae3fcebb7c2d32d8f95270421e1671906e3
---
 AndroidManifest.xml | 11 ++++++-----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/AndroidManifest.xml b/AndroidManifest.xml
index 2534911..d3a0049 100755
--- a/AndroidManifest.xml
+++ b/AndroidManifest.xml
@@ -185,11 +185,12 @@
             android:label="@string/quick_reader_name"
             android:theme="@style/AppTheme" />
 
-        <receiver android:name="com.android.camera.DisableCameraReceiver">
-            <intent-filter>
-                <action android:name="android.intent.action.BOOT_COMPLETED" />
-            </intent-filter>
-        </receiver>
+        <!-- BOOT_COMPLETED trigger removed (see device/samsung/sltexx patches): on sltexx
+             the receiver's Camera1 enumeration returns 0 cameras at boot, which permanently
+             disabled the CameraLauncher icon after every fresh flash, while the camera is
+             present and works. The camera2 mode it also set is computed by CameraActivity
+             itself at every start, so nothing else depended on this receiver. -->
+        <receiver android:name="com.android.camera.DisableCameraReceiver"/>
         <receiver android:name="com.android.camera.CameraButtonIntentReceiver">
             <intent-filter>
                 <action android:name="android.intent.action.CAMERA_BUTTON"/>
-- 
